25	// Multiple-BFS based estimation of the graph radii (vertex eccentricities).
26	//
27	// 64 breadth-first searches are run simultaneously from 64 sampled source
28	// vertices; the set of sources that have reached a vertex is stored as a
29	// bitmask in a single 64-bit word (Visited/NextVisited).  A vertex's radii
30	// value is the last round in which its bitmask grew, i.e. the distance to the
31	// furthest sampled source that reaches it.  The maximum over all vertices is
32	// therefore a lower-bound estimate of the graph's diameter/radius.
